    "watt": {
      "definition": "Rated power at STC",
      "unit": "W",
      "type": "number"
    },
    "voc": {
      "definition": "Open-circuit voltage (stringing input to the controller; rises in cold)",
      "unit": "V",
      "type": "number"
    },
    "vmp": {
      "definition": "Voltage at max power point",
      "unit": "V",
      "type": "number"
    },
    "isc": {
      "definition": "Short-circuit current",
      "unit": "A",
      "type": "number"
    },
    "cells": {
      "definition": "Cell count / class",
      "type": "number"
    },
    "form": {
      "definition": "Physical type",
      "type": "enum",
      "values": [
        "rigid",
        "foldable"
      ]
    },
    "condition": {
      "definition": "New / used / surplus",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "dollars_per_w": {
      "definition": "Approximate price per watt",
      "unit": "USD/W",
      "type": "number"
    },
    "price_usd": {
      "definition": "Approximate price per panel/unit (verify)",
      "unit": "USD",
      "type": "number"
    },
    "source": {
      "definition": "Reference URL",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "mass_kg": {
      "definition": "Mass of one unit/block (feeds system_mass_kg)",
      "unit": "kg",
      "type": "number"
    },
    "area_m2": {
      "definition": "Physical panel area (feeds array_area_m2)",
      "unit": "m2",
      "type": "number"
    },
    "temp_coeff_pmax": {
      "definition": "Temperature coefficient of Pmax (negative; feeds cell-temperature derate). Datasheet where available, else typical for the cell class.",
      "unit": "%/degC",
      "type": "number"
    },
    "noct": {
      "definition": "Nominal Operating Cell Temperature / NMOT (feeds cell-temp estimate). Datasheet where available.",
      "unit": "degC",
      "type": "number"
    }
  },
  "guidance": [
    "Monocrystalline default. Larger 60/72-cell 'residential' panels give the best $/W; small 12 V-nominal panels cost more per watt but suit tiny/RV builds.",
    "SF Bay Craigslist has used 300-315 W residential panels at ~$0.14-0.18/W (~$45-55). That's the very good end of the ~$0.05-0.60/W used market. Facebook Marketplace is login-walled (search it yourself).",
    "Foldable/suitcase panels run $1-2/W (the portability tax) but pack down, self-stand, no glass \u2014 good for a 1-week desert teardown.",
    "Stringing ceiling is the controller's max PV Voc, not the battery bus. Cold-Voc rule: Voc_cold = Voc_STC x (1 + (T_min - 25) x -0.003). Two 40 V-Voc panels in series can approach a 100 V MPPT limit on a cold morning.",
    "Higher string voltage (more in series) = lower current = thinner PV wire. Keep all panels in a string the same model so the string isn't dragged to the weakest panel.",
    "On playa: stake/ballast against wind and wipe dust daily (dust = lost watts). Inspect used panels for cracks/delamination/burnt junction box; confirm MC4 vs cut leads."
  ],
